    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59647" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραν-τήρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραίνω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one that accomplishes</i>:
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραντῆρες, οἱ</span>, <i>wisdom-teeth</i>, which come last and
				<i>complete the set</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				501b25
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κριτῆρες</span> cited by <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				742.37
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.93
			</span></i>: generally, <i>teeth</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				447
			</span></i> (sg.), <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Onom.</u>
				51
			</span></i>: in sg., a boar's <i>tusk</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				833
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>ruler</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραντῆρα βοῶν ταῦρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>A.</u>
					313
				</span></i>
			.</div>
